  "published": "2026-10-28T07:28:27.53Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "- Breaking: `Stop()` is final - it used to keep the manager usable, and a system resume after the app's `Stop()` started location detection again on its own, beside the next manager the app initialized (two request loops on one backend session). A resume now restarts only what the suspend paused; call `UserLocationManager.InitializeAsync` again to detect locations after `Stop()`\n- Breaking: add `Permissions.Camera` (\"AR Video\") for parity with iOS and Android; the numeric values of `Permissions.ArHardware` and `Permissions.UwbHardware` changed. Windows never reports it (camera-based motion tracking is reported as `Permissions.ArHardware`)\n- Add `UserLocationManager.ResetSession()` and `UserLocationManager.SessionId`: an app can start a new backend session, so the backend calculates from scratch instead of continuing from what the old session held. Readings collected for the old session are dropped; the client id stays\n- Add opt-in diagnostics: `LocationDetectionDiagnostics.SetHandler(Action<string>?)` gets every request body sent to the positioning backend (`→ <body>`) and its answer (`← <status> <body>`, also for non-200 responses, or `← error: <message>` for network errors and timeouts), one line each. Nothing is built without a handler; the API key is never written\n- Fix the backend's `must_restart` keeping the readings collected for the old session: they are now dropped together with the session\n- Fix a stop scheduled by a suspend that could still run when the system resumed just as the 2 s ran out: cancelling it (on resume or by `Stop()`) now always drops it\n- Send one mean RSSI per beacon and second instead of every single BLE advertisement - the request carried dozens of readings per beacon. Readings without an RSSI (0 or 127) are dropped, and `txPower` is the beacon's last advertised measured power\n- The configuration and the backend session are now behind a lock, as the scanners and the request loop read them from different threads",
